{
    "_comment": [
        "CANONICAL FORMS — NOT a node capture (unlike every other zpool-status fixture here).",
        "The real stunt/fleet captures cover the common scan records already:",
        "  zpool-status-online.json      SCRUB / FINISHED, processed 0B, 0 errors  ('scrub repaired 0B in ... with 0 errors on ...')",
        "  zpool-status-resilvering.json RESILVER / FINISHED                       ('resilvered 18K in ... with 0 errors on ...')",
        "  zpool-status-scrubbing.json   SCRUB / SCANNING, end_time '-'            ('scrub in progress since ...')",
        "  zpool-status-online-fresh.json  no scan_stats at all                    ('scan: none requested')",
        "What no capture contains is a scrub that actually REPAIRED something, a scrub that",
        "found errors, and a CANCELED scrub ('zpool scrub -s') — producing those on demand",
        "means damaging a real pool. The two pools below are those forms, written in the",
        "field shape the captures above prove OpenZFS emits (same keys, same value syntax:",
        "human sizes, ctime dates, string counts). Provenance is documented so nobody mistakes",
        "them for observed output; if a live one is ever captured, replace these with it.",
        "'processed' is the field ZFS's own 'repaired %s' text prints, and the duration ZFS",
        "prints as 'in %s' is end_time - start_time."
    ],
